      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of 850 mg to 1,000 mg.\n- A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, for 2,550 mg/day. This is the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- Another dose, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. I'd advise against that, though."
      }
     ],
