     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Metformin 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled daily dose. No indication I know of supports that dose, and it carries a real risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or 1,000 mg PO twice daily. I can enter either one now.\n- **Discuss with your attending or a clinical pharmacist** if you think this patient needs an off-label dose. If they agree, the order can be placed through the appropriate channel with the rationale documented.\n- **Check the source of the dose.** The number may have come from a transcription or unit error, or from a different formulation or drug.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
